        <body>
            <div xml:id="d551-a2">

                <pb facs="0647" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg575"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">official notice.</hi></head>
                <p>Mahmoud Chevket Pasha, commanding the army of occupation, requests all the
                    inhabitants of the places declared in a state of siege who are carrying or who
                    have in their houses prohibited arms of any kind to carry them to the nearest
                    police station in Constantinople and to the commanders of the army in the sand
                    jacks, and to deliver them to the above authorities against a receipt.</p>
                <p>At the expiration of this time, viz, five days from date, any persons who may be
                    found with arms or ammunition in their possession, either on their persons or in
                    their houses, will be considered as disturbers of public order and punished as
                    such by court-martial.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="rumi gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nissan</hi>, 21,
                            1325.<lb/>(May 5, 1909.)</date></dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
